 "note": "XS, 14 platforms, mirrored both ways. A strait runs down the middle; ONE ferry serves its three crossings and sits on the top, middle, bottom, middle lane in turn (time your send to the lane it is heading for). The dry ways over are the two stones, top and bottom - each a laser LIFT: DOWN it joins the two outer roads, UP the two banks' end platforms (the top one starts down, the bottom one up). Each home's straight middle road is a belt toward the strait. Finale: the two banks, split by the ferry.",
 "geometricSymmetry": true,
 "experimental": false,
 "ruleWaivers": {
  "L05": "the finale's decision is the ferry between the banks (a hazard on its own clock: when to send, which lane); the rulebook's stand-in reads a hazard ferry as a fixed deck, so L05 cannot see it (round R, 2026-11-05)",
  "R07": "Daniele 2026-11-05: two mirrored laser lifts, top and bottom - each stone has an equally short twin, so firing one alone never moves the shortest length (the other stone carries it); together they decide which roads cross dry",
  "R04": "Daniele 2026-11-05 merge (stone above AND below the 3-lane strait over 2 m half decks): 67.5 m tall, 1.5 m over the provisional 66 m line; the phone probe decides (plan rule 7)"
 },
